# Wendy Planner — committed dev defaults (OPS-023).
#
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  PURPOSE
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# This file externalizes the application's runtime configuration so that
# the source code stays free of environment-specific values (host names,
# ports, issuer names, TTLs, etc.). It is **committed to git** on purpose
# and should only carry **non-sensitive** values that typically do NOT
# change between environments (development, staging, production):
#
#   • host names / ports / log levels
#   • external service identifiers (issuer, audience)
#   • non-secret timing / size / capacity knobs (TTLs, thresholds, limits)
#   • local development credentials that match docker-compose.yml
#     (e.g. POSTGRES_USER/PASSWORD/DB = wendy/wendy/wendy)
#
# Anything sensitive — private keys, signing secrets, real production
# credentials, third-party API tokens — belongs in **.env.local**, which
# is git-ignored and overrides this file on a per-developer basis.
#
# NestJS ConfigModule loads the chain (first hit wins):
#   1. <monorepo-root>/.env.local
#   2. <monorepo-root>/.env          ← this file
#   3. apps/api/.env.local
#   4. apps/api/.env
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ─── Runtime ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
NODE_ENV=development
PORT=3000
LOG_LEVEL=log

# ─── Database (ADR-16, ARC-008) ──────────────────────────────────────────
# Matches POSTGRES_USER/PASSWORD/DB in docker-compose.yml. `localhost`
# is correct because docker-compose publishes the Postgres port
# 5432:5432 to the host. Do NOT use the in-network DNS name here —
# this file is read by the host-side CLI process (pnpm dev / start:dev),
# not by a container in the compose network.
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://wendy:wendy@localhost:5432/wendy?schema=public
